Source: ownfs
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Will Rouesnel <wrouesnel@wrouesnel.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ownfs-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: ownfs
Description: ownership-squashing stacked filesystem (DKMS module source)
 ownfs mounts a Linux filesystem such as ext4, XFS, btrfs or f2fs so that
 every file appears to belong to the user who mounted it, the way FAT, exFAT
 and NTFS drives behave. New files are stored on disk as the owner of the
 drive's top-level directory.
 .
 This package provides the kernel module source, built for each installed
 kernel by DKMS.

Package: ownfs
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ownfs-dkms (= ${binary:Version}), udisks2 (>= 2.9)
Description: removable Linux filesystems owned by the desktop user
 Makes udisks2 mount removable drives (USB, SD cards and FireWire) that carry
 ext2/3/4, XFS, btrfs or f2fs through ownfs, so the desktop user can read and
 write everything on them regardless of the user and group IDs stored on
 disk, just as with FAT, exFAT and NTFS drives. Internal disks are not
 affected.
